**Definition 22.1 (block Time).** Let $\mathcal H_{\rm blk}$ consist
of the actual block/gap histories

$$
h=K^{q_0}B_1K^{q_1}\cdots B_mK^{q_m},
\qquad m\ge1,
\tag{22.1}
$$

where each $B_i$ is an independent block on its actual predecessor,
$q_0,q_m\ge0$, and $q_i\ge1$ for $1\le i<m$.
Also admit $h=K^{q_0}$ for $m=0$. Each block records its addressed
typed set and forgets the chosen internal permutation. Put
$n=\sum_i|B_i|$ and $Q=\sum_iq_i$; then $I(t)=n$, the number of
individual births, rather than $m$.

Starting at the paid scalar seed one, actually execute the block
members and Ticks. Write $F_{\rm blk}(h)=(t(h),x_h)$.
Theorem 21.2 makes this independent of block enumeration.
As in Definition 3.2, Reads, Holds, refusals, framing and waiting
are not letters of this Time. Their actual costs remain if present.
No chosen serial shuffle or old word is handed to the decoder.

